    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Three things, stated plainly so you know which parts of this page are reads and which are reconstruction.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. The three digits of the symbol-counting puzzle.</b> The dials were read at five separate seconds between 2:18 and 2:30 and the passes disagreed: the whole-frame read gave <b>3 4 2</b> and a 2.4x crop of the same second gave <b>2 4 3</b>. The dials are being turned while the camera is on them, so a single second is not a reliable state. This page therefore prints no final answer for the star, ring and chair counts — count them yourself in the room, and if your dials agree with either reading you are almost certainly right.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. What 7435 is for.</b> The number is solid — three independent reads, three crop scales, all agreeing — but nothing in the decodable part of the recording types it anywhere. It may be the crate code in a different build, the balance target, or a clue for the white box. We are not going to invent a lock for it, and we are certainly not going to swap it with the 7432 that the crate demonstrably takes.
      <br><br>
      <b>3. The ending and the reward.</b> The file is 3:20 long and the last frame is the terrace at 3:18 with sparkles. No results card, no <i>level completed</i> banner, no coin figure. Any reward number you see quoted for the Terrace did not come from this recording.
